      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Classification of Rivers of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Indian river systems are broadly divided into Himalayan and Peninsular systems.",
        "The Himalayan System includes major networks like the Ganga and its important tributaries.",
        "Peninsular rivers are categorized into East-flowing and West-flowing rivers based on their drainage direction.",
        "Drainage patterns and major river valley projects/dams play a critical role in regional hydrography."
      ],
      "id": "51fontj"
    },
